{"entries":[{"caption":"Figure 1. Survey coverage by site and year. Each tile is a site-year that has at least one survey. Colour shows how many surveys met the completeness rule (≥ 80% of planned quadrats, metadata present). The number is the total surveys that year. Only sites visited in two or more different years are shown. There are no files for 2009–2015 or 2021–2023.","key":"fig-coverage","order":{"number":1,"section":[0,6,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Figure 2. How filtering changes coverage. Number of surveys per year that remain as quality filters are added one after another: (1) all surveys with a date and site; (2) quadrat-level data exist (not just a compiled summary); (3) effort metadata present and plausible. The gap between lines is the data each filter removes.","key":"fig-filtering","order":{"number":2,"section":[0,6,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["question-and-metrics","data-inventory","cleaning-decisions","exclusions-log","duplicates-log","cross-check-against-the-compiled-sheet","clean-master-data-preview","reusable-function-check_effort","figures","open-questions-for-opihi","ai-use"]}